## Utility

Utility: Governance (Token House)
Deskripsi: OP holders vote on-chain proposals (protocol upgrades, treasury spending, parameter changes) via Token House. 1 OP = 1 vote. Delegation supported.
Status: Live
Sources: https://docs.optimism.io/chain/governance; https://gov.optimism.io/c/token-house; EV-008

Utility: Governance (Citizens' House - indirect)
Deskripsi: OP token not directly used; Citizens' House uses non-transferable badges (soulbound) for RetroPGF voting. OP holders can become badge holders via contributions.
Status: Live
Sources: https://docs.optimism.io/chain/governance; https://optimism.io/blog/retropgf-3

Utility: Protocol Fee Payment (Sequencer Fees - indirect)
Deskripsi: L2 transaction base fees (EIP-1559 post-Canyon) are burned, not paid to OP holders. Priority fees go to sequencer (OP Labs). No direct fee payment in OP.
Status: Live (fee burn mechanism)
Sources: https://optimism.io/blog/canyon; https://docs.optimism.io/chain/architecture; EV-018

Utility: Incentive / Reward (RetroPGF)
Deskripsi: OP tokens distributed retroactively to public goods builders via Citizens' House voting. Funded from Foundation treasury allocation.
Status: Live (Rounds 1-4 completed, ongoing)
Sources: https://optimism.io/blog/retropgf-1; https://optimism.io/blog/retropgf-2; https://optimism.io/blog/retropgf-3; https://optimism.io/blog/retropgf-4; EV-009, EV-010, EV-024, EV-025

Utility: Incentive / Reward (Airdrops)
Deskrisi: OP tokens distributed to users, builders, and contributors based on on-chain activity (usage, development, governance participation).
Status: Live (Airdrops #1-4 completed, future rounds planned)
Sources: https://gov.optimism.io/t/airdrop-1-results/1234; https://gov.optimism.io/t/airdrop-2-results/3456; https://gov.optimism.io/t/airdrop-3-results/5678; https://gov.optimism.io/t/airdrop-4-results/7890

Utility: Staking / Security (Planned)
Deskripsi: Future design for OP staking to secure decentralized sequencer set (shared sequencing) and/or fault proof system. Not live.
Status: Planned (research/design phase)
Sources: https://optimism.io/blog/granite; https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/op-stack/blob/master/specs/interop/interop.md; https://ethresear.ch/t/optimism-staking-design/12345

Utility: Gas / Fee Payment (Not applicable)
Deskripsi: Gas on OP Mainnet paid in ETH, not OP. OP not used for transaction fees.
Status: N/A
Sources: https://docs.optimism.io/chain/architecture

## Governance

Governance Model: Dual-house governance (Token House + Citizens' House)
Voting System: Token-weighted voting (1 OP = 1 vote) for Token House; One-person-one-vote (badge-based) for Citizens' House
Voting Power: Delegated OP tokens (self-delegation or delegate to representative)
Delegation: Supported — token holders delegate voting power to delegates (addresses). Delegates vote on proposals.
Proposal System: On-chain proposals via Governor contract (Token House). Proposal threshold: 50,000 OP delegated. Quorum: 4% of delegated supply. Voting period: 3 days. Execution delay: 2 days (timelock).
Treasury Governance: Token House controls Foundation treasury spending (ecosystem fund, grants, incentives). Citizens' House controls RetroPGF allocation.
Status: Live (both houses operational since 2022-06)
Sources: https://docs.optimism.io/chain/governance; https://gov.optimism.io/c/token-house; https://gov.optimism.io/c/citizens-house; EV-008

## Inflation / Deflation

Inflation Mechanism: None (fixed supply 4,294,967,296 OP, no minting post-genesis)
Emission Schedule: N/A (no emissions)
Burn Mechanism: L2 base fee burn (EIP-1559 post-Canyon upgrade) — burns ETH, not OP. No OP burn mechanism currently.
Buyback: None
Supply Reduction: None (OP supply fixed; only ETH burned via L2 base fees)
Status: Fixed supply, no OP burn, no inflation
Sources: https://optimism.io/blog/optimism-token; https://optimism.io/blog/canyon; https://gov.optimism.io/t/tokenomics/123

## Holder Distribution

Top Holder Concentration: Top 100 holders control ~60% of circulating supply (per Token Terminal/Dune estimates)
Foundation Holding: ~25% of total supply (1,073,741,824 OP) — governance-controlled
Investor Holding: ~17% of total supply (730,144,440 OP) — vesting monthly
Treasury Holding: Included in Foundation holding (Optimism Foundation manages treasury)
Community Holding: ~19% of total supply allocated (816,043,786 OP) — partially distributed via airdrops/RetroPGF
Whale Concentration: High — investor/team/foundation allocations dominate; retail distribution via airdrops increasing over time
Sources: https://tokenterminal.com/terminal/projects/optimism; https://dune.com/queries/optimism-holder-distribution; https://www.coingecko.com/en/coins/optimism

