## Open Threads

- Exact circulating supply as of current date — CoinGecko/Token Terminal estimates vary; no official real-time dashboard from Foundation
- RetroPGF Round 4 exact OP amount — blog post announces round completion but does not disclose nominal allocation
- Airdrop #5+ plans — Foundation has signaled future airdrops but no timeline or criteria published
- OP staking design specifics — ethresear.ch discussions exist but no formal specification or governance proposal finalized
- Investor/team vesting exact unlock schedule per month — aggregate 17% each vesting over 4 years but monthly unlock amounts not published in machine-readable format
- Foundation treasury current OP balance — not publicly disclosed in real-time; only governance proposals show spending amounts
- Ecosystem fund deployment rate — Token House proposals show individual grants but no aggregate spending dashboard
- Whether any OP tokens have been burned (accidental or intentional) — no burn mechanism exists but need to verify no anomalous burns on-chain
- Citizens' House badge holder count and OP holder overlap — badge holders not required to hold OP; correlation unknown
- Delegation participation rate — percentage of OP supply actively delegated vs. idle not published in official metrics
- Legal classification of OP token (utility vs. security) — Foundation maintains utility classification but no regulatory no-action letter published
- Cross-chain OP token representation (OP on Ethereum L1, Base, other OP Stack chains) — canonical token only on OP Mainnet L2; bridged versions exist but not officially tracked